  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/181d0bd8-7012-4e7f-b605-09c878298df5-image.png\" style=\"width: 213px; height: 120px;\" /></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> be resistance of galvanometer and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;be the current passing through the galvanometer produces full scale deflection. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> is the maximum current, and since, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> are in parallel so, the potential difference between them will be same.</p><p>Then,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>72</mn><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math></p><p>So the percentage of total current passes through galvanometer&nbsp;is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mi>I</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mrow><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>",
